the target language is: prolog.

% Minimal reproduction of prepositional-chain answer folding and ordering.
% - "we will make *a payment*" is a normal template.
% - "under" and "in respect of" are prepositional, so a chained instance
%   ("we will make ... under ... in respect of ...") compiles to a main literal
%   plus one prepositional goal per phrase.
% Query 1 exercises: (1) no leading "true and", (2) the rule head's prepositional
% goals compile in textual order (under before in respect of), (3) the answer is
% re-folded into the compact sentence rather than the unfolded conjunction.

the templates are:
    we will make *a payment*.
    *a payment* under *a policy*; prepositional.
    *a payment* in respect of *a claim*; prepositional.
    *a payment* is valid.

the knowledge base folding includes:
    we will make a payment under this policy in respect of a claim
        if the payment is valid.

scenario zero is:
    this payment is valid.
    this payment under this policy.
    this payment in respect of this claim.
    1 expects answers ["we will make this payment under this policy in respect of this claim"].

query 1 is:
    we will make which payment under this policy in respect of this claim.
